/******************************************************************************************
 *
 * File:        qlik_load_script.qvs
 * Project:     Cash Pooling Proof of Concept
 * Platform:    Qlik Sense Cloud
 *
 * Author:      Alexandre de Andrade
 * Purpose:     Initial ETL load script for the Cash Pooling PoC.
 *
 * Description:
 * This script implements the first stage of the ETL process:
 * - Loading crude (raw) CSV data
 * - Preserving source structure and granularity
 * - Establishing a governed foundation for further transformations
 *
 * Design Principles:
 * - Separation of concerns
 * - Traceability and reprocessability
 * - Clear distinction between data layers
 *
 * IMPORTANT:
 * At this stage, NO business rules, aggregations or derived metrics
 * are applied. All transformations will be introduced incrementally
 * and documented.
 *
 ******************************************************************************************/

/*==============================================================================
  0. ENVIRONMENT & SCRIPT SETTINGS
==============================================================================*/

/*
Decision:
Explicitly define script environment settings to avoid implicit defaults
that may vary across environments or developers.

Rationale:
Improves predictability, readability and portability of the script.
*/

SET ThousandSep=',';
SET DecimalSep='.';
SET MoneyThousandSep=',';
SET MoneyDecimalSep='.';
SET MoneyFormat='$#,##0.00;-$#,##0.00';
SET TimeFormat='hh:mm:ss';
SET DateFormat='YYYY-MM-DD';
SET TimestampFormat='YYYY-MM-DD hh:mm:ss[.fff]';
SET FirstWeekDay=0;
SET BrokenWeeks=0;
SET ReferenceDay=0;
SET FirstMonthOfYear=1;


/*==============================================================================
  1. DATA SOURCE PARAMETERS
==============================================================================*/

/*
Decision:
Centralize file paths and parameters at the beginning of the script.

Rationale:
- Simplifies maintenance
- Enables quick redirection to other environments
- Is a standard practice in governed ETL pipelines
*/

LET vRawDataPath = 'lib://data/raw/';


/*==============================================================================
  2. RAW (CRUDE) DATA LOAD
==============================================================================*/

/*
This section loads data exactly as provided by the source CSV files.

Decision:
No transformations, no joins, no calculations at this stage.

Rationale:
- Preserves data lineage
- Enables full reload and reprocessing
- Aligns with data lake / lakehouse concepts
*/


/*------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  2.1 Company Master Data
------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

Companies_Raw:
LOAD
    company_code,
    company_name,
    parent_company,
    country,
    local_currency
FROM [$(vRawDataPath)companies.csv]
(txt, utf8, embedded labels, delimiter=',', msq);


/*
Decision:
Keep company hierarchy attributes in the raw layer.

Rationale:
Hierarchy logic will be applied later, but source attributes must
remain untouched for transparency and auditability.
*/


/*------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  2.2 Cost Center Master Data
------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

CostCenters_Raw:
LOAD
    cost_center,
    cost_center_name,
    company_code,
    country
FROM [$(vRawDataPath)cost_centers.csv]
(txt, utf8, embedded labels, delimiter=',', msq);


/*------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  2.3 Country Reference Data
------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

Countries_Raw:
LOAD
    country,
    region,
    reporting_currency
FROM [$(vRawDataPath)countries.csv]
(txt, utf8, embedded labels, delimiter=',', msq);


/*------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  2.4 Currency Reference Data
------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

Currencies_Raw:
LOAD
    currency,
    currency_name,
    exchange_rate_to_group
FROM [$(vRawDataPath)currencies.csv]
(txt, utf8, embedded labels, delimiter=',', msq);


/*------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  2.5 Treasury Cash Position (Fact – Crude)
------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

CashPosition_Raw:
LOAD
    company_code,
    company_name,
    country,
    cost_center,
    fiscal_year,
    fiscal_month,
    currency,
    opening_balance,
    cash_in,
    cash_out,
    closing_balance,
    pooling_scenario
FROM [$(vRawDataPath)treasury_cash_position.csv]
(txt, utf8, embedded labels, delimiter=',', msq);


/*
Decision:
Load the cash position table as a single, non-aggregated fact dataset.

Rationale:
- Monthly grain is preserved
- Pre/Post pooling scenarios coexist in the same structure
- Enables flexible analytical slicing later
*/


/*==============================================================================
  3. HOUSEKEEPING & SCRIPT CONTROL
==============================================================================*/

/*
Decision:
Explicitly separate raw data load from transformation logic.

Rationale:
This makes the script easier to read, review and evolve incrementally.
Subsequent sections will:
- Rename tables
- Apply transformations
- Build the analytical model
*/


/*
Temporary end of initial version.
Further ETL steps will be added in controlled iterations.
*/

/******************************************************************************************
 *
 * GOVERNED DIMENSIONS
 *
 * Scope:
 * - Create governed dimension tables (Dim_*)
 * - Preserve raw data integrity
 * - Prepare the analytical model foundation
 *
 ******************************************************************************************/

/*==============================================================================
  4. GOVERNED DIMENSIONS
==============================================================================*/

/*
Decision:
Introduce governed dimensions as separate logical entities (Dim_*),
derived from raw datasets.

Rationale:
- Clear separation between source data and analytical structures
- Improves readability and maintainability
- Aligns with enterprise BI modeling practices
*/


/*------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  4.1 Company Dimension
------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

/*
Decision:
Create a single Company dimension containing both entity attributes
and hierarchical information (parent company).

Rationale:
- Enables standalone and consolidated analysis
- Avoids pre-aggregation
- Reflects real-world multinational corporate structures
*/

Dim_Company:
LOAD DISTINCT
    company_code,
    company_name,
    parent_company,
    country            AS company_country,
    local_currency
RESIDENT Companies_Raw;


/*
Decision:
Keep hierarchy fields (parent_company) directly in the dimension.

Rationale:
- Simplifies consolidation logic later
- Avoids separate hierarchy tables at this PoC stage
*/


/*------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  4.2 Cost Center Dimension
------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

/*
Decision:
Model Cost Centers as a governed dimension linked to Company.

Rationale:
- Cost centers are stable master data
- They define analytical slicing for treasury monitoring
*/

Dim_CostCenter:
LOAD DISTINCT
    cost_center,
    cost_center_name,
    company_code,
    country            AS cost_center_country
RESIDENT CostCenters_Raw;


/*------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  4.3 Country Dimension
------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

/*
Decision:
Create an explicit Country dimension, even if attributes are minimal.

Rationale:
- Enables geographical analysis
- Supports future regional aggregation
- Improves semantic clarity in the data model
*/

Dim_Country:
LOAD DISTINCT
    country,
    region,
    reporting_currency
RESIDENT Countries_Raw;


/*------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  4.4 Currency Dimension
------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

/*
Decision:
Model Currency as a dimension rather than embedding attributes
directly in the fact table.

Rationale:
- Centralizes exchange rate governance
- Facilitates controlled currency conversion
- Avoids duplication of reference data
*/

Dim_Currency:
LOAD DISTINCT
    currency,
    currency_name,
    exchange_rate_to_group
RESIDENT Currencies_Raw;


/*==============================================================================
  5. RAW DATA CLEANUP (OPTIONAL)
==============================================================================*/

/*
Decision:
At this stage, raw tables are intentionally kept in memory.

Rationale:
- Allows validation and comparison between raw and governed layers
- Useful during PoC development and debugging

Raw tables may be dropped in a later optimization step.
*/


/*
End of Version 2.
Next steps will introduce:
- Calendar dimension
- Fact table creation
- Currency conversion logic
*/
